{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>And I will remember My covenant with Jacob</b> — with Isaac 'remembering' is not written, for his ashes are gathered and laid before HaKadosh Baruch Hu. The patriarchs are listed in reverse: HaKadosh Baruch Hu says, I remember whence you came, and I count and trace the lineage upward, to son of Jacob son of Isaac son of Abraham. In all of them 'אף' is written, except Jacob, for his bed was whole and no waste issue issued from him. 'And I will remember' — the verse begins with remembrance and ends with remembrance, for the merit of the fathers is remembered forever. Abraham is called His servant, as written, 'Remember for Your servants,' and adjacent to it 'Abraham'; and likewise with Jacob it is written, 'Jacob My servant' — but not so with Isaac, for Abraham and Jacob fulfilled the commandments both in the Land and outside the Land, but not so Isaac. Abraham and Jacob are mentioned as head of the patriarchs, and Isaac is not mentioned anywhere as head, because the intent was that to Esau he would be 'a master to your brother,' to make him head over Jacob."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:20:54.853378619Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}